This product includes a modified copy of the default seccomp profile of the
Moby project: drydock_eval/contain/reference/lib/seccomp_g4s_d41.json is
derived from seccomp/default.json of github.com/moby/profiles (module version
v0.2.3), which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The profile originates in the Moby project (github.com/moby/moby), whose NOTICE
file reads:

    Docker
    Copyright 2012-2017 Docker, Inc.

    This product includes software developed at Docker, Inc.
    (https://www.docker.com).

At the time of packaging, the repository github.com/moby/profiles had no NOTICE
file of its own, and the profile file carries no copyright line. The text above
is the notice of the Moby project and is carried here as the nearest upstream
attribution. The Moby NOTICE also names two other components; neither is part
of this product.

Changes made to the profile: the Linux native AIO system calls (io_setup,
io_destroy, io_submit, io_cancel, io_getevents, io_pgetevents and
io_pgetevents_time64) were removed from the allow rules, and one rule was added
that returns EPERM for them and for io_uring_setup, io_uring_enter and
io_uring_register. The derivation is reproducible with
drydock_eval/contain/reference/tools/make_seccomp_d41.py; the added rule is the
last entry of "syscalls" in the profile. The profile file itself is shipped
byte for byte as generated, because the contained runner pins its sha256, so
this statement of change lives here and not inside the file.
